  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0042","idiomatic","Earlier Empress Rende and Empress Dowager Qintian were estranged; Qintian secretly set Anren to spy on the empress's every move, and nothing escaped him.","Earlier Empress Rende and Empress Dowager Qin'ai were estranged; Qin'ai secretly set Anren to spy on the empress's every move, and nothing escaped him.","Chinese 欽哀 is Qin'ai; Qintian misreads 哀 as tian. The proposed Empress Dowager Qin'ai restores the correct temple-name reading without changing the rest of the sentence.","high","applied"],
    ["s0042","literal","Earlier, Empress Rende and Qintian were at odds; Qintian secretly ordered Anren to watch the empress's movements—nothing escaped his knowledge.","Earlier, Empress Rende and Qin'ai were at odds; Qin'ai secretly ordered Anren to watch the empress's movements—nothing escaped his knowledge.","The literal field likewise renders 欽哀 as Qintian; Qin'ai is the accurate pinyin, and the rest of the literal rendering matches 與欽哀有隙 / 欽哀密令安仁.","high","applied"],
    ["s0044","idiomatic","Rende sought to have him executed, but Qintian interceded for him.","Rende sought to have him executed, but Qin'ai interceded for him.","In 仁德欲誅之，欽哀以言營救 the intercessor is 欽哀 (Qin'ai), not Qintian; the proposed swap corrects the name only.","high","applied"],
    ["s0044","literal","Rende wished to execute him; Qintian pleaded on his behalf.","Rende wished to execute him; Qin'ai pleaded on his behalf.","Same unit: 欽哀 is Qin'ai; replacing Qintian in the literal line is a real transliteration fix, not a stylistic change.","high","applied"],
    ["s0048","idiomatic","Early in the Chongxi era Empress Dowager Qintian served as regent, sought to depose the emperor, and planned to enthrone her younger son Chongyuan.","Early in the Chongxi era Empress Dowager Qin'ai served as regent, sought to depose the emperor, and planned to enthrone her younger son Chongyuan.","重熙初，欽哀攝政 names the regent as 欽哀 (Qin'ai); Empress Dowager Qintian is a mistransliteration, and the proposed Empress Dowager Qin'ai is accurate.","high","applied"],
    ["s0048","literal","At the beginning of Chongxi, Qintian acted as regent, wished to depose the emperor, and install her younger son Chongyuan.","At the beginning of Chongxi, Qin'ai acted as regent, wished to depose the emperor, and install her younger son Chongyuan.","The literal likewise misreads 欽哀 as Qintian; Qin'ai correctly names the regent who 欲廢帝，立少子重元.","high","applied"]
